1484:We have shown that assuming the exponential time hypothesis there are solvable groups with equation satisfiability problem not decidable in polynomial time. Thus, under standard assumptions from complexity theory this means a negative answer to \cite[Problem 1]{BurrisL04} (also conjectured in \cite{Horvath11}). \cref{thm:main2} yields a quasipolynomial time lower bound under ETH. Thus, a natural weakening of \cite[Problem 1]{BurrisL04} is as follows:
